  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), る-ending.\n- Negative: {羽織|はお}らない\n- Polite: {羽織|はお}ります\n- Te-form: {羽織|はお}って\n- Past: {羽織|はお}った\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed specifically for outer garments or coverings worn loosely over the shoulders. Not used for putting on pants, shoes, or tightly fitted clothing. The related noun {羽織|はおり} is a traditional Japanese jacket worn over a kimono.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {上着|うわぎ}を{羽織|はお}る: to throw on a jacket\n- コートを{羽織|はお}る: to throw on a coat\n- {肩|かた}に{羽織|はお}る: to drape over one's shoulders",
